{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate_repository(root)` MUST return a report with the number of discovered requirements, the number of discovered examples, the number of evidence files, and all validation errors for the supplied project. Ordinary invalid evidence MUST be reported in that report; an inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. The text has three obligations. `validate_repository` must return the counts and all validation errors. Ordinary invalid evidence must be reported in the report. An inaccessible root must return an I/O error.\n\n**Code**\n- `src/evidence.rs#fn[validate_repository]` returns `inspect_repository(root)?.report`. It calls `inspect_repository_with_progress`, which `inspect_repository` wraps.\n- `src/evidence.rs#struct[EvidenceReport]` carries `requirements`, `examples`, `evidence_files` and `errors`.\n- `src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` fills those fields:\n  - It counts definitions of kind `Requirement` and kind `Example` separately.\n  - It sets `evidence_files` to the number of discovered evidence files.\n  - It pushes every validation finding into `errors`. This covers config, book and definition errors, per-file evidence errors, orphan evidence, missing evidence, reference, citation, site and coverage errors.\n  - It does not return `Err` for invalid evidence.\n- The root is opened with `fs::canonicalize(root)?` as the first step. An inaccessible root therefore returns `Err`, while ordinary evidence problems stay in `errors`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Counts and an empty `errors`: `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` and `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates`. The latter asserts 1 requirement, 1 example and 2 evidence files.\n- Errors collected in the report: `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` asserts a long list of error messages. `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` asserts further errors after each mutation. The `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` test `discovered_external_cargo_outputs_validate_freshness_and_obey_disallow` asserts errors for changed and disallowed inputs.\n- An I/O error for an inaccessible root: `inaccessible_project_root_is_an_io_error_not_a_report` asserts `NotFound` for a missing root. It also asserts that invalid evidence in an accessible root appears in `report.errors`.\n- `inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase` and `fixme_fixture` add further coverage of the report fields.\n\nI found no unspecified extra behavior in the `{impl}` items.",
